Date: 2026-10-07 (updated 2026-10-18)

This fork of the CSE 507 course repository (https://github.com/jliangclass-intro/2026Fall-CSE507-Ark-Container)
modifies Ark+ code from JLiangLab/Ark (https://github.com/JLiangLab/Ark), which reaches this fork through the course
repository (the course's Ark+ container code) and is licensed under the ASU license reproduced in LICENSE-ASU-Ark.txt;
the course repository itself has no license file. This file describes the changes, as section 5(c) of that license
requires. The changes are relative to the course repository's main branch at commit
2949b2e764b11e21c31d668efcc10cf2a33acd20. The modified Python and shell sources listed below begin with a header
comment pointing here.

Modified files inherited from the course repository

- base/engine.py: adds layer-wise LR decay parameter groups for the DINO ViTs, --eval_every, --clip-grad wiring and a grouped-optimizer resume check; the frozen-backbone phase (--freeze_backbone), the cycle-0 weights and evaluation (--eval_cycle0), the input size recorded in the saved weights and checked on resume and in test mode, and the test result file suffix of the offline evaluation protocols.
- base/joint_training.py: the joint-training loop measures or clips the gradient norm before each optimizer step and logs it (GN).
- base/main_ark.py: adds the vit_base_dinov3, vit_base_dinov2, vit_base_raddino and vit_large_raydino model choices, the raddino and none normalizations, and the --eval_every, --layer-decay, --patch-embed-lr-mult, --eval_cycle0, --freeze_backbone and --test_output_suffix options; test mode takes --input_size and --img_resize from the saved weights.
- base/models.py: adds ArkViT (DINOv3 ViT-B/16 with projector and heads), ArkViTDinoV2 (the DINOv2 ViT for DINOv2, RAD-DINO and RayDINO weights), vit_param_groups, and a strict check of the loaded checkpoint keys; build_omni_model_from_checkpoint refuses a checkpoint without the requested key, checks a Swin checkpoint's embed_dim, window and input size against the model, and checks the loaded keys.
- base/trainer.py: the cyclic training loop measures or clips the gradient norm before each optimizer step and logs it (GN).
- base/utils.py: adds clip_or_measure_grad_norm.
- experiment_scripts/common.sh: the shared launcher reads batch size, lr, warmup epochs, test augmentation, evaluation cadence, cycle-0 evaluation, input size, resize, workers, model, init and pretrained weights from ARK_* environment variables; the defaults reproduce the original behavior.
- base/dataloader.py: adds the raddino normalization preset (RAD-DINO's grayscale mean and std).
- plot/compare_cyclic_runs.py, plot/plot_cyclic_run.py, plot/run_labels.py, plot/README.md: mAUC plotted in percent, the cycle-0 (init) point, --models, --full-length, --colors and --labels, and fixed labels for the Demo 1 and sweep arms.
- README.md: prepends "About this fork", replaces the container download command with a pointer to the course repository's README, and appends "Gaudi on Sol".
- .gitignore: also ignores weights/, *.pth, *.pt, *.safetensors, .DS_Store and *.log, the SSL run checkpoints and exports, and the linear-probe embedding caches and logs.

Added files

New tools in base/
- base/check_dinov3_load.py: CPU smoke test for the vit_base_dinov3 backbone.
- base/convert_hf_dinov3_to_meta.py: converts a Hugging Face DINOv3 ViT-B/16 checkpoint to Meta's state-dict layout.
- base/test_dinov3_finetune_recipe.py: CPU checks for the DINOv3 fine-tuning recipe (AdamW, layer-wise LR decay, grad-norm clipping).
- base/convert_safetensors_to_pth.py, base/make_cycle0_weights.py, base/weight_norms.py, base/probe_resolution_memory.py, base/probe_ssl_memory.py: a safetensors-to-.pth converter, the cycle-0 weights of runs trained before --eval_cycle0, per-block weight norms, and the one-card memory probes for the fine-tune input sizes and the SSL crop sizes.
- base/test_*.py (chain scripts, offline evaluation, frozen backbone, DINOv2 backbone, SSL trainer, the two probes): CPU tests.

Stage A SSL continued pretraining (DINO-X)
- base/ssl_pretrain.py and base/ssl_dinov3/: DINOv3-style SSL continued pretraining of the ViT-B/16 backbone on chest X-rays (student, EMA teacher, Gram teacher), on the vendored DINOv3 loss, data and train modules.
- chain/: the Stage A phase scripts that run_d1_8_chain_gaudi.sh runs back to back in one allocation (chain/README.md), with the gate (gate.py) and its tests.
- sweep/: the fine-tuning sweep table (wave1.tsv) and its submitter.
- plot/plot_linear_probes.py, plot/build_step8_report.py, plot/NAMING-RULES.md: the linear-probe figure, the DINO-X report builder (workbook, figures, deck, ledger tables) and the naming rules its outputs follow.

Vendored Meta code, under its own license
- base/dinov3/: the DINOv3 ViT and the SSL loss, data and train modules from https://github.com/facebookresearch/dinov3, licensed under the DINOv3 License (base/dinov3/LICENSE.md); base/dinov3/VENDORED.md records the source commit and which files were edited or are ours.
- base/dinov2/: the DINOv2 ViT from https://github.com/facebookresearch/dinov2, licensed under the Apache License 2.0 (base/dinov2/LICENSE); base/dinov2/VENDORED.md records the source and the one edited file.

Ported Ark code, under the ASU license
- base/ark_finetune/ and base/ark_linearprobe/: ports of the Ark+ fine-tuning data code (dataloader.py) and embedding linear probe (main_linearprobing.py, utils.py) from https://github.com/jlianglab/Ark (Ark_Plus/Finetuning, Ark_Plus/Linearprobing), with our embedding extractor and probe runner around them; each directory has its own LICENSE (the ASU license) and a NOTICE that describes the changes.

Gaudi2 (HPU) path
- containers/gaudi/: apptainer.def, requirements.txt and requirements_nodeps.txt for the Gaudi2 container.
- gaudi.sh: runs a command inside the Gaudi container (the counterpart of nvidia.sh).
- gaudi_hlsmi.sh, gaudi_check_cards.sh, gaudi_verify_busy.sh: the shared hl-smi reader, the fail-closed pre-launch card check, and the report-only busy check.
- gaudi_smoke.sh: 1-card smoke test.
- build_gaudi_image.sh: builds containers/gaudi/gaudi.sif.

Experiment scripts and launchers
- experiment_scripts/all4_concurrent_random_sampling/, all4_concurrent_random_sampling_dinov3/, all4_cyclic_dinov3_adamw/, all4_cyclic_dinov3_v2/, all4_cyclic_dinov3_short/, all4_cyclic_dinov3_frozen/, all4_cyclic_dinov3_frozen_long/, all4_cyclic_dinov3_probe/ and all4_cyclic_dinov3_sweep/: start and resume scripts for the Demo 1 runs on all four datasets (VinDr-CXR, ChestX-ray14, MIMIC, CheXpert).
- run_p1_*.sh and resume_p1_*.sh in the repository root: Slurm launchers for the Practice 1 runs.
- run_d1_*.sh, resume_d1_*.sh and eval_d1_6.sh in the repository root: Slurm launchers for the Demo 1 runs and the d1_6 evaluation, including the Gaudi launchers (run_d1_8*_gaudi.sh, resume_d1_8a_gaudi.sh, resume_d1_8c_gaudi.sh: the arms, the Stage A chain driver, the sweep arms on 2, 4 and 8 cards, the DINO-X ConstLR 512 px Gram-512 twin, a timing job), run_emb_gaudi.sh (the linear probe), run_probe_resolution_gaudi.sh and run_probe_ssl_gaudi.sh (the memory probes), and weight_norms.sh.
- run_emb_class.sh in the repository root: Slurm launcher for the linear probe on one A100 of the class account, the sibling of run_emb_gaudi.sh (the same arguments, checks and fit, through nvidia.sh).

Documentation
- docs/gaudi-vs-a100.md, docs/gaudi-vs-a100.pdf, docs/sol-gaudi-guide.md, docs/sol-gaudi-guide.pdf: the short and the long guide to running the training on Sol's Gaudi2 cards.

